    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look to capitalize on high-upside matchups today, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson**, who leads the squad with an elite 81.88 efficiency score. Facing a favorable matchup against a right-handed arm with a 4.41 xERA, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive 16% park adjustment and an ideal spot in the three-hole, making him our cornerstone play. **Drake Baldwin** also earns a prime start at catcher (71.83); his leadoff role combined with a significant park-factor boost against a middle-of-the-road starter makes him a high-floor producer today. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** (71.56) is a lock in the outfield, bolstered by a 13% platoon efficiency gain and favorable SP metrics that allow him to drive the offense from the five-spot.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, whose 47.58 score fell just short of our threshold. While **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** possesses the talent to flip a game, his struggle against left-handed pitching\u2014driving a 15% drop in his platoon projection\u2014made him less efficient than options like **Nasim Nunez** or **Dominic Smith** in this specific rotation. We are closely monitoring wind conditions for **Denzer Guzman**; while his base score is marginal, the projected wind-out boost pushes him into the starting lineup to exploit a soft 6.03 xERA matchup. Meanwhile, **Kyle Tucker** (59.20) and **Andy Pages** (55.84) face slight headwinds from negative BvP history and the opposing catcher\u2019s elite pop time, respectively, but their projected volume keeps them in the mix as we hunt for runs and RBI. \n\nOwners should note that while **Heliot Ramos** (55.10) is slotted into the lineup, he carries a situational risk due to the opposing pitcher\u2019s ability to suppress stolen bases\u2014a category where we prioritize efficiency above all else. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** remains a sturdy play (63.39), though his outlook is tempered slightly by a \"Wind In\" advisory at the park, which could mute his HR potential against the opposing lefty. Proceed with confidence in our top-tier trio, but keep a close eye on the late-afternoon weather reports affecting **Denzer Guzman** and **Heliot Ramos** to ensure their situational advantages hold.",
